{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996471-mopaditis-clan","id":996471,"title":"Mopaditis Clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T23:41:18-07:00","id":996471,"title":"Mopaditis Clan","content":"<u><b>Mopaditis Clan</b></u><br /> Kindred have never been common in the sunburnt country. Many believe that the Australia had never felt the touch of the Beast before british colonists came. But in the northern reaches of the outback there is an old story of people who died alone.<br /> <br /> Some tales have it that their legs were injured by a crocodile or bunyip while hunting and couldn\u2019t walk back to their people before dusk fell, while others say they were a troublemaker who was thrown out as a result of their tricks and fell down a cliff because of the darkness. How they died isn\u2019t important, what is important was that they were alone when they died, and yet they heard a voice while they gave their final breath. The wild spirit spoke of a gift, that it could grant them a second chance at life, a second chance to be amongst people, a second chance to be with their friends. Those that accept were returned by generous the power of this spirit, though they were required to sleep in caves during the day and thirsted for blood of the living.<br /> <br /> To ward off these lonely predators, some kurditcha learned how to ritually conjure spirits of smoke. Such rites were troublesome though, as the entities themselves required sacrifice before they would lend any aid. In the modern day, the Mopaditis have realised they are kin with many others, not only seeing themselves as kindred with other vampires, but also with the Kurditcha and the Bound. Though the Mopaditis are still rare enough that many of the Australian supernaturals they consider family have no idea they even exist.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane (Forever Alone)</b>: The beast gave Mopaditis a second chance to connect with people, so when these undead waste their \u201cgift\u201d the beast grows angry at the foolish kindred. Failing a social roll is treated as a +1 provocation/circumstance modifier for frenzy, -1 if a dramatic failure. A frenzy caused by this provocation generally has escape as it's goal.<br /> <b>Nickname</b>: Stalkers<br /> <b>Favoured Attributes:</b> Composure or Presence<br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Celerity, <i>Protean</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Inspiration</b>: <i>I saw a website which talked about Mopaditis as undead spirits who followed people around but were scared off by smoke or by person shouting at the spirit.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 06-09-2017, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:11:29-07:00","id":996966,"title":"","content":"Given how the game works, I think you should make this a Bloodline instead of a new clan. Given that the very origins of each clan is as muddy as it is, this wouldn't even require to assume a common ancestor with the rest of the clan. Clan affinity for Blood Empathy could be just similar Curses or Beasts recognizing one another.<br /> <br /> I would suggest Daeva, though the description could also be easily Gangrel or Mekhet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:26:48-07:00","id":996974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996471-mopaditis-clan?p=996966#post996966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how the game works, I think you should make this a Bloodline instead of a new clan. Given that the very origins of each clan is as muddy as it is, this wouldn't even require to assume a common ancestor with the rest of the clan. Clan affinity for Blood Empathy could be just similar Curses or Beasts recognizing one another.<br /> <br /> I would suggest Daeva, though the description could also be easily Gangrel or Mekhet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I prefer the fact that Kindred are like convergent evolution, their clans may come from different origins but they all end up with similar traits in the end. Also bloodlines seem horrible for this to me, since the number of vampires in pre-colonial australia would be ridiculously tiny + the immense distances between those vampires would mean that they generally never meet each other, so how did all of them end up joining this bloodline if contact between each other is so immensely rare?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:08:11-07:00","id":996991,"title":"","content":"If one considers the following post canon there's certainly merit for having a whole new clan on other continents: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/705402-vampires-in-the-neolithic?p=710162\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ithic?p=710162</a><br /> <br /> By the time of the Vin\u010da culture clans had not yet been codified. The first migration to Australia took place at least 35000 years earlier so if the Mopaditis was around before Western exploration and colonization it would make more sense for them being a clan rather than a bloodline of clans they couldn't have spread from.<br /> <br /> Still, it's not a published text so I don't think it's the official canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:25:12-07:00","id":996997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996471-mopaditis-clan?p=996974#post996974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I prefer the fact that Kindred are like convergent evolution, their clans may come from different origins but they all end up with similar traits in the end. Also bloodlines seem horrible for this to me, since the number of vampires in pre-colonial australia would be ridiculously tiny + the immense distances between those vampires would mean that they generally never meet each other, so how did all of them end up joining this bloodline if contact between each other is so immensely rare?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that's what I meant.<br /> <br /> Being them like Convergent Evolution, a clan doesn't need to be made of real relatives, but instead of similar monsters. And maybe at this level the blood just call for such similarity. And there are many ways for those monsters in particular to have developed what is <u>mechanically</u> the &quot;same bloodline&quot;. If they're Embraced, it can simply be in their blood. If they were, at some point, each a unique creature, the bloodline could manifest from the way they were created.<br /> <br /> If true blood relation were necessary to be of a common clan, then there would be far more than 5 clans. To me, they aren't about <i>just</i> blood relation, but about the underlying Beast recognizing a being of similar nature. And bloodlines, for me, handle the rest perfectly fine, including this kind of phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:49:32-07:00","id":997004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996471-mopaditis-clan?p=996997#post996997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that's what I meant.<br /> <br /> Being them like Convergent Evolution, a clan doesn't need to be made of real relatives, but instead of similar monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have different views on what Convergent Evolution means in Requiem. I can see them evolving to all be considered Kindred, but I don't really see why an exact clan would duplicate to such a severe extent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And maybe at this level the blood just call for such similarity. And there are many ways for those monsters in particular to have developed what is <u>mechanically</u> the &quot;same bloodline&quot;. If they're Embraced, it can simply be in their blood. If they were, at some point, each a unique creature, the bloodline could manifest from the way they were created. </div> </div> </div>To me, it sounds a lot less of a stretch that they are 1 clan which happens to be a separate one to the ones the rest of the world has everywhere because of how isolated Australia was, rather than they are all 1 clan which is the exact same as this other clan on the other side of the planet And they All have a unique bloodline to represent that they are separate to the rest of the world because of how isolated Australia was....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If true blood relation were necessary to be of a common clan, then there would be far more than 5 clans. To me, they aren't about <i>just</i> blood relation, but about the underlying Beast recognizing a being of similar nature. And bloodlines, for me, handle the rest perfectly fine, including this kind of phenomenon. </div> </div> </div>Well, there are more than just five. I mean, there are six in VtR alone (nine if you count the lost ones), and in chapter 1 it talks about how new clans do appear over time rather than it just being five archetypal clans.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't really see how the existing clans really fit. Daeva and Venture would auto-win socialness with dominate and majesty, gangrels are savage not timid, mekhet and nosferatu wouldn't ever be noticed by those they stalk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-02-2016, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:55:21-07:00","id":997006,"title":"","content":"Ok, I can live with some &quot;creative differences&quot;. I know there are more than 5 possible clans, but from here the distinction is in meaningless details.<br /> <br /> But on the Gangrel, I would like to add: you're just stereotyping them, here. The other clans really would have those characteristics because of their in-clan disciplines. But the Gangrel don't have to be savages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}